# @comment-ok: the rail contract, the single doc site for what this report means.
# report_extract.dl6 -- sprefa-extract reading its OWN Rust source, in process.
#
# THE LOOP, in one read:
#
#   want(glob)                         one /arrivals row names the corpus
#     -> files(glob, path, digest)     SoopyFilesExecutor, linked, no git child
#     -> source_file(path, digest)
#     -> df_node_at / df_edge_at / call_node_at / type_node_at
#                                      SprefaExtractExecutor, LINKED: the
#                                      extractor runs inside the engine process
#                                      and $DL_EXTRACT_BIN is never spawned.
#                                      Four named projections, identical
#                                      templates, so the applicative fold
#                                      serves all four from ONE run per file
#                                      (hosts.rs is_applicative). `cst` is
#                                      deliberately absent from the family
#                                      list: this report needs the callable
#                                      and type entity planes, and the cst
#                                      plane is ~6x the row volume.
#     -> df_node / df_edge / proc_def / type_def
#     -> df_reach + df_hop             the in-tick MUTUAL closure (PR #266).
#                                      Neither head reads ITSELF, so
#                                      lower.pl's direct-self-read test leaves
#                                      both with ExpandPlan=none and the
#                                      closure comes entirely from the outer
#                                      rounds. This is the path/reach shape of
#                                      conformance/fixtures/24_mutual_recursion.pl
#                                      on real extracted edges.
#     -> chain_level + chain_step      the second mutual pair, depth-capped
#     -> node_owner_start              innermost owner = the containing
#                                      callable with the greatest start, one
#                                      max aggregate over the containment
#                                      pairs rather than the
#                                      not(smaller_owner(...)) anti-join
#                                      flagship-flow.dl6 spells, which is a
#                                      third join over the same pairs
#     -> report_markdown(...)          markdown TEXT, assembled by group_concat
#
# Its rx lowering, per the "every snippet carries its lowering" law. Every
# fan-out is one more mergeMap over rows; there is no nested subscription and
# no per-file lifetime:
#
#   wantRows$.pipe(map(mintIdentityAndWitness), distinct(r => r.witnessDigest),
#                  mergeMap(runLinkedFiles), mergeMap(commitEdbArrival))
#
#   sourceFile$.pipe(map(mintIdentityAndWitness), distinct(r => r.witnessDigest),
#                    mergeMap(runLinkedExtract), mergeMap(commitEdbArrival))
#
#   dfEdge$.pipe(expand(row => joinAgainstReach(row)), distinct(rowKey))
#                                                     // = df_reach / df_hop
#
#   sectionLine$.pipe(groupBy(row => row.sectionOrdinal),
#                     mergeMap(g => g.pipe(toArray(),
#                                          map(lines => lines.sort().join('\n')))))
#                                                     // = the group_concat wraps
#
# dl6 WRITES NO FILE. fs effects are unbuilt, so `report_markdown` is queried
# and redirected by the wrapper (v6/dl/dataflow/report-extract.sh).
#
# ASSEMBLY follows the Phase F rendered_type precedent: a *_line rel per table,
# a group_concat wrap per table, one wrap rule per section. group_concat with
# TWO arguments orders by the VALUE (lower.pl aggregate_select_expr), so a line
# whose leading field is the sort key needs no ordinal column; the two ranked
# tables carry an int ordinal and take the three-argument spelling.
#
# EVERY per-file count carries a ZERO ARM. An aggregate over an empty group
# produces no row, and a file with no callables must still appear in the
# inventory.
#
# @comment-ok: the rail contract continues; this paragraph is the identity law.
# NODE IDENTITY IS (span, kind), AND THE WIRE NOW SPELLS BOTH. `FlatFact::Edge`
# carries `from_kind`/`to_kind` beside the endpoint spans, and the Rust lift
# stores each value node's full extent, so every rel below that names a node
# names all three columns. Two nodes may still share a span (an implicit `ret`
# covers the tail expression it returns); the kind is what keeps them apart, and
# `aliased_span` in section 5 prices how often that happens.
#
# TWO MEASURED LIMITS THIS RAIL DEGRADES AROUND rather than faking:
#
#   1  INTERPROCEDURAL FLOW IS UNBUILT. types.rs `DfEdgeKind` carries only
#      `Direct`; the `Flow` union (arg->param, ret->call_res, higher-order) is
#      commented out and marked PENDING. So every edge here is
#      intra-procedural and no chain crosses a callable. Section 6 states that
#      as a TODO row instead of inventing a cross-proc hop.
#   2  GO AND KOTLIN VALUE NODES ARE STILL START-ONLY, `go.rs` / `kotlin.rs`
#      df_push with `len: 0`. @comment-ok: one paragraph per named limit.
#      Pointing this rail at a .go or .kt corpus brings the merged nodes and
#      their invented cycles back. 32 is the ladder's termination guard, a
#      LITERAL in the `chain_step` guard and nowhere else; on the Rust corpus
#      the graph is a DAG whose longest chain is well under it, so a reported
#      depth is measured, never saturated.

rel span(start: int, end: int).

# `/soopy/files` is the rel name IS the executor binding (registry.pl
# arrival_executor/2), routed to SoopyFilesExecutor, linked, no git child.
rel /soopy/files(glob: text) -> (path: text, digest: text).

rel /extract/df_node_at(path: text, digest: text, families: text) -> (record: text, family: text, span: span, kind: text) key(1, 3).
rel /extract/df_edge_at(path: text, digest: text, families: text) -> (record: text, family: text, kind: text, from: span, from_kind: text, to: span, to_kind: text) key(1, 3).
rel /extract/call_node_at(path: text, digest: text, families: text) -> (record: text, family: text, span: span, kind: text, name: text) key(1, 3).
rel /extract/type_node_at(path: text, digest: text, families: text) -> (record: text, family: text, span: span, kind: text, name: text) key(1, 3).

rel want(glob: text).

rel source_file(path: text, digest: text).
source_file(Path, Digest) <- want(Glob), /soopy/files(Glob, Path, Digest).

# A JSONL line missing a declared column contributes no row, so `name: text`
# is itself the filter that keeps anonymous callables out.
rel df_node(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text).
df_node(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind) <-
  source_file(Path, Digest),
  /extract/df_node_at(Path, Digest, "type,call,df", 'node', 'df', NodeAt, NodeKind),
  decode(NodeAt, {start: NodeStart, end: NodeEnd}).

# The endpoint KINDS are the second half of df node identity; without them two
# nodes at one span are one graph node and the closure below invents cycles.
rel df_edge(path: text, from_start: int, from_end: int, from_kind: text,
            to_start: int, to_end: int, to_kind: text).
df_edge(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind) <-
  source_file(Path, Digest),
  /extract/df_edge_at(Path, Digest, "type,call,df", 'edge', 'df', 'direct', FromAt, FromKind, ToAt, ToKind),
  decode(FromAt, {start: FromStart, end: FromEnd}),
  decode(ToAt, {start: ToStart, end: ToEnd}).

rel proc_def(path: text, proc_start: int, proc_end: int, proc_name: text).
proc_def(Path, ProcStart, ProcEnd, ProcName) <-
  source_file(Path, Digest),
  /extract/call_node_at(Path, Digest, "type,call,df", 'node', 'call', ProcAt, _ProcKind, ProcName),
  decode(ProcAt, {start: ProcStart, end: ProcEnd}).

rel type_def(path: text, type_start: int, type_end: int, type_kind: text, type_name: text).
type_def(Path, TypeStart, TypeEnd, TypeKind, TypeName) <-
  source_file(Path, Digest),
  /extract/type_node_at(Path, Digest, "type,call,df", 'node', 'type', TypeAt, TypeKind, TypeName),
  decode(TypeAt, {start: TypeStart, end: TypeEnd}).

rel df_reach(path: text, from_start: int, from_end: int, from_kind: text,
             to_start: int, to_end: int, to_kind: text).
rel df_hop(path: text, from_start: int, from_end: int, from_kind: text,
           to_start: int, to_end: int, to_kind: text).

df_reach(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind) <-
  df_edge(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind).
df_reach(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind) <-
  df_hop(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind).
df_hop(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind) <-
  df_reach(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, MiddleStart, MiddleEnd, MiddleKind),
  df_edge(Path, MiddleStart, MiddleEnd, MiddleKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind).

rel cyclic_value(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text).
cyclic_value(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind) <-
  df_reach(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind).

rel df_target(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text).
df_target(Path, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind) <- df_edge(Path, _, _, _, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind).

rel chain_root(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text).
chain_root(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind) <-
  df_node(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind),
  not(df_target(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind)).

rel chain_level(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text, level: int).
rel chain_step(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text, level: int).

chain_level(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, 0) <-
  chain_root(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind).
chain_level(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, Level) <-
  chain_step(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, Level).
chain_step(Path, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind, NextLevel) <-
  chain_level(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, Level),
  Level < 32,
  df_edge(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind),
  NextLevel := Level + 1.

# An aggregate's group columns must be bound by EACH positive body atom's own
# delta (lower.pl:4312), so every join under one feeds a materialized rel first.
rel node_proc_candidate(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text,
                        proc_start: int).
node_proc_candidate(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, ProcStart) <-
  df_node(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind),
  proc_def(Path, ProcStart, ProcEnd, _),
  NodeStart >= ProcStart,
  NodeEnd =< ProcEnd.

rel node_owner_start(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text,
                     proc_start: int).
node_owner_start(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, max(ProcStart)) <-
  node_proc_candidate(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, ProcStart).

rel node_proc(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, node_kind: text,
              proc_start: int, proc_name: text).
node_proc(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, ProcStart, ProcName) <-
  node_owner_start(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, ProcStart),
  proc_def(Path, ProcStart, _, ProcName).

rel proc_node_count(path: text, proc_start: int, nodes: int).
proc_node_count(Path, ProcStart, count(NodeStart)) <-
  node_proc(Path, NodeStart, _, _, ProcStart, _).

# The target columns are what make a row an EDGE: dropping them would make this
# rel a set of source nodes and the count below would report those instead.
rel proc_edge(path: text, proc_start: int, from_start: int, from_end: int, from_kind: text,
              to_start: int, to_end: int, to_kind: text).
proc_edge(Path, ProcStart, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind) <-
  df_edge(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ToStart, ToEnd, ToKind),
  node_proc(Path, FromStart, FromEnd, FromKind, ProcStart, _).

rel proc_edge_count(path: text, proc_start: int, edges: int).
proc_edge_count(Path, ProcStart, count(FromStart)) <-
  proc_edge(Path, ProcStart, FromStart, _, _, _, _, _).

rel proc_node_level(path: text, proc_start: int, node_start: int, node_kind: text, level: int).
proc_node_level(Path, ProcStart, NodeStart, NodeKind, Level) <-
  chain_level(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, Level),
  node_proc(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind, ProcStart, _).

rel proc_depth(path: text, proc_start: int, depth: int).
proc_depth(Path, ProcStart, max(Level)) <-
  proc_node_level(Path, ProcStart, _, _, Level).

# One rel cannot carry both an aggregate head and a plain head (lower.pl:3891),
# so each zero arm is its own rel: `*_seen` counts, `*_none` supplies the zero.
rel has_proc(path: text).
has_proc(Path) <- proc_def(Path, _, _, _).
rel file_proc_seen(path: text, procs: int).
file_proc_seen(Path, count(ProcStart)) <- proc_def(Path, ProcStart, _, _).
rel file_proc_none(path: text, procs: int).
file_proc_none(Path, 0) <- source_file(Path, _), not(has_proc(Path)).
rel file_proc_count(path: text, procs: int).
file_proc_count(Path, Procs) <- file_proc_seen(Path, Procs).
file_proc_count(Path, Procs) <- file_proc_none(Path, Procs).

rel has_type(path: text).
has_type(Path) <- type_def(Path, _, _, _, _).
rel file_type_seen(path: text, types: int).
file_type_seen(Path, count(TypeStart)) <- type_def(Path, TypeStart, _, _, _).
rel file_type_none(path: text, types: int).
file_type_none(Path, 0) <- source_file(Path, _), not(has_type(Path)).
rel file_type_count(path: text, types: int).
file_type_count(Path, Types) <- file_type_seen(Path, Types).
file_type_count(Path, Types) <- file_type_none(Path, Types).

rel has_df_node(path: text).
has_df_node(Path) <- df_node(Path, _, _, _).
rel file_node_seen(path: text, df_nodes: int).
file_node_seen(Path, count(NodeStart)) <- df_node(Path, NodeStart, _, _).
rel file_node_none(path: text, df_nodes: int).
file_node_none(Path, 0) <- source_file(Path, _), not(has_df_node(Path)).
rel file_node_count(path: text, df_nodes: int).
file_node_count(Path, Nodes) <- file_node_seen(Path, Nodes).
file_node_count(Path, Nodes) <- file_node_none(Path, Nodes).

rel has_df_edge(path: text).
has_df_edge(Path) <- df_edge(Path, _, _, _, _, _, _).
rel file_edge_seen(path: text, df_edges: int).
file_edge_seen(Path, count(FromStart)) <- df_edge(Path, FromStart, _, _, _, _, _).
rel file_edge_none(path: text, df_edges: int).
file_edge_none(Path, 0) <- source_file(Path, _), not(has_df_edge(Path)).
rel file_edge_count(path: text, df_edges: int).
file_edge_count(Path, Edges) <- file_edge_seen(Path, Edges).
file_edge_count(Path, Edges) <- file_edge_none(Path, Edges).

rel has_reach(path: text).
has_reach(Path) <- df_reach(Path, _, _, _, _, _, _).
rel file_reach_seen(path: text, reachable_pairs: int).
file_reach_seen(Path, count(FromStart)) <- df_reach(Path, FromStart, _, _, _, _, _).
rel file_reach_none(path: text, reachable_pairs: int).
file_reach_none(Path, 0) <- source_file(Path, _), not(has_reach(Path)).
rel file_reach_count(path: text, reachable_pairs: int).
file_reach_count(Path, Pairs) <- file_reach_seen(Path, Pairs).
file_reach_count(Path, Pairs) <- file_reach_none(Path, Pairs).

rel has_cyclic(path: text).
has_cyclic(Path) <- cyclic_value(Path, _, _, _).
rel file_cyclic_seen(path: text, cyclic_nodes: int).
file_cyclic_seen(Path, count(NodeStart)) <- cyclic_value(Path, NodeStart, _, _).
rel file_cyclic_none(path: text, cyclic_nodes: int).
file_cyclic_none(Path, 0) <- source_file(Path, _), not(has_cyclic(Path)).
rel file_cyclic_count(path: text, cyclic_nodes: int).
file_cyclic_count(Path, Cyclic) <- file_cyclic_seen(Path, Cyclic).
file_cyclic_count(Path, Cyclic) <- file_cyclic_none(Path, Cyclic).

# df_node is a SET, so two facts at one span survive only when their kinds
# differ; the count is over the WHOLE span, which is what an edge endpoint names.
rel span_kind_count(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int, kinds: int).
span_kind_count(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, count(NodeKind)) <-
  df_node(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, NodeKind).

rel aliased_span(path: text, node_start: int, node_end: int).
aliased_span(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd) <-
  span_kind_count(Path, NodeStart, NodeEnd, Kinds), Kinds > 1.

rel has_aliased_span(path: text).
has_aliased_span(Path) <- aliased_span(Path, _, _).
rel file_aliased_seen(path: text, aliased_spans: int).
file_aliased_seen(Path, count(NodeStart)) <- aliased_span(Path, NodeStart, _).
rel file_aliased_none(path: text, aliased_spans: int).
file_aliased_none(Path, 0) <- source_file(Path, _), not(has_aliased_span(Path)).
rel file_aliased_count(path: text, aliased_spans: int).
file_aliased_count(Path, Aliased) <- file_aliased_seen(Path, Aliased).
file_aliased_count(Path, Aliased) <- file_aliased_none(Path, Aliased).

rel file_distinct_span_seen(path: text, distinct_spans: int).
file_distinct_span_seen(Path, count(NodeStart)) <- span_kind_count(Path, NodeStart, _, _).
rel file_distinct_span_none(path: text, distinct_spans: int).
file_distinct_span_none(Path, 0) <- source_file(Path, _), not(has_df_node(Path)).
rel file_distinct_span_count(path: text, distinct_spans: int).
file_distinct_span_count(Path, Spans) <- file_distinct_span_seen(Path, Spans).
file_distinct_span_count(Path, Spans) <- file_distinct_span_none(Path, Spans).

rel total_files(files: int).
total_files(count(Path)) <- source_file(Path, _).
rel total_procs(procs: int).
total_procs(count(ProcStart)) <- proc_def(_, ProcStart, _, _).
rel total_types(types: int).
total_types(count(TypeStart)) <- type_def(_, TypeStart, _, _, _).
rel total_df_nodes(df_nodes: int).
total_df_nodes(count(NodeStart)) <- df_node(_, NodeStart, _, _).
rel total_df_edges(df_edges: int).
total_df_edges(count(FromStart)) <- df_edge(_, FromStart, _, _, _, _, _).
rel total_reach(reachable_pairs: int).
total_reach(count(FromStart)) <- df_reach(_, FromStart, _, _, _, _, _).
# A corpus total needs the same zero arm a per-file count does: with the graph
# acyclic and no span aliased, the seen arm is empty and the section would vanish.
rel cyclic_anywhere(present: int).
cyclic_anywhere(1) <- cyclic_value(_, _, _, _).
rel total_cyclic_seen(cyclic_nodes: int).
total_cyclic_seen(count(NodeStart)) <- cyclic_value(_, NodeStart, _, _).
rel total_cyclic_none(cyclic_nodes: int).
total_cyclic_none(0) <- total_files(_), not(cyclic_anywhere(_)).
rel total_cyclic(cyclic_nodes: int).
total_cyclic(Cyclic) <- total_cyclic_seen(Cyclic).
total_cyclic(Cyclic) <- total_cyclic_none(Cyclic).

rel aliased_anywhere(present: int).
aliased_anywhere(1) <- aliased_span(_, _, _).
rel total_aliased_seen(aliased_spans: int).
total_aliased_seen(count(NodeStart)) <- aliased_span(_, NodeStart, _).
rel total_aliased_none(aliased_spans: int).
total_aliased_none(0) <- total_files(_), not(aliased_anywhere(_)).
rel total_aliased(aliased_spans: int).
total_aliased(Aliased) <- total_aliased_seen(Aliased).
total_aliased(Aliased) <- total_aliased_none(Aliased).

# Competition ranking: rank = how many procs are strictly wider, so a tie
# shares one rank and a cut at `Rank < N` never drops half a tied group.
rel wider_pair(path: text, proc_start: int, other_path: text, other_start: int).
wider_pair(Path, ProcStart, OtherPath, OtherStart) <-
  proc_node_count(Path, ProcStart, Nodes),
  proc_node_count(OtherPath, OtherStart, OtherNodes),
  OtherNodes > Nodes.

rel wider_proc(path: text, proc_start: int).
wider_proc(Path, ProcStart) <- wider_pair(Path, ProcStart, _, _).

rel proc_rank_widest(path: text, proc_start: int, rank: int).
proc_rank_widest(Path, ProcStart, 0) <-
  proc_node_count(Path, ProcStart, _), not(wider_proc(Path, ProcStart)).
rel proc_rank_below(path: text, proc_start: int, rank: int).
proc_rank_below(Path, ProcStart, count(OtherStart)) <-
  wider_pair(Path, ProcStart, _, OtherStart).
rel proc_rank(path: text, proc_start: int, rank: int).
proc_rank(Path, ProcStart, Rank) <- proc_rank_widest(Path, ProcStart, Rank).
proc_rank(Path, ProcStart, Rank) <- proc_rank_below(Path, ProcStart, Rank).

rel depth_histogram(depth: int, procs: int).
depth_histogram(Depth, count(ProcStart)) <- proc_depth(_, ProcStart, Depth).

rel file_line(line_text: text).
file_line(LineText) <-
  source_file(Path, _),
  file_proc_count(Path, Procs),
  file_type_count(Path, Types),
  file_node_count(Path, Nodes),
  file_edge_count(Path, Edges),
  LineText := concat(['| `', Path, '` | ', Procs, ' | ', Types, ' | ', Nodes, ' | ', Edges, ' |']).

rel file_table(body: text).
file_table(group_concat(LineText, '\n')) <- file_line(LineText).

rel reach_line(line_text: text).
reach_line(LineText) <-
  source_file(Path, _),
  file_edge_count(Path, Edges),
  file_reach_count(Path, Pairs),
  file_cyclic_count(Path, Cyclic),
  LineText := concat(['| `', Path, '` | ', Edges, ' | ', Pairs, ' | ', Cyclic, ' |']).

rel reach_table(body: text).
reach_table(group_concat(LineText, '\n')) <- reach_line(LineText).

rel proc_line(rank: int, line_text: text).
proc_line(Rank, LineText) <-
  proc_rank(Path, ProcStart, Rank),
  Rank < 25,
  proc_node_count(Path, ProcStart, Nodes),
  proc_edge_count(Path, ProcStart, Edges),
  proc_depth(Path, ProcStart, Depth),
  proc_def(Path, ProcStart, _, ProcName),
  LineText := concat(['| `', Path, '` | `', ProcName, '` | ', Nodes, ' | ', Edges, ' | ', Depth, ' |']).

rel proc_table(body: text).
proc_table(group_concat(LineText, '\n', Rank)) <- proc_line(Rank, LineText).

rel depth_line(depth: int, line_text: text).
depth_line(Depth, LineText) <-
  depth_histogram(Depth, Procs),
  LineText := concat(['| ', Depth, ' | ', Procs, ' |']).

rel depth_table(body: text).
depth_table(group_concat(LineText, '\n', Depth)) <- depth_line(Depth, LineText).

rel alias_line(line_text: text).
alias_line(LineText) <-
  source_file(Path, _),
  file_node_count(Path, Nodes),
  file_distinct_span_count(Path, DistinctSpans),
  file_aliased_count(Path, Aliased),
  LineText := concat(['| `', Path, '` | ', Nodes, ' | ', DistinctSpans, ' | ', Aliased, ' |']).

rel alias_table(body: text).
alias_table(group_concat(LineText, '\n')) <- alias_line(LineText).

# `section_ordinal` is what the wrapper sorts on; `section_name` is the handle
# a shell selection uses to name one section.
rel report_markdown(section_ordinal: int, section_name: text, section_text: text).

report_markdown(0, 'header', SectionText) <-
  total_files(Files),
  total_procs(Procs),
  total_types(Types),
  total_df_nodes(Nodes),
  total_df_edges(Edges),
  SectionText := concat([
    '# sprefa-extract dataflow, extracted by sprefa-extract\n',
    '\n',
    'Generated by `v6/dl/dataflow/report_extract.dl6` on the Rust door.\n',
    'The extractor ran LINKED, inside the engine process: the `sprefa_extract`\n',
    'execution tag routes to `SprefaExtractExecutor`, so no `extract` child was\n',
    'spawned and `$DL_EXTRACT_BIN` was never resolved.\n',
    '\n',
    '| corpus | value |\n',
    '|---|--:|\n',
    '| files | ', Files, ' |\n',
    '| callable definitions | ', Procs, ' |\n',
    '| type entities | ', Types, ' |\n',
    '| df value nodes | ', Nodes, ' |\n',
    '| df Direct edges | ', Edges, ' |\n']).

report_markdown(1, 'inventory', SectionText) <-
  file_table(Body),
  SectionText := concat([
    '## Corpus inventory\n',
    '\n',
    '| file | procs | types | df nodes | df edges |\n',
    '|---|--:|--:|--:|--:|\n',
    Body, '\n']).

report_markdown(2, 'reachability', SectionText) <-
  reach_table(Body),
  total_reach(Pairs),
  total_cyclic(Cyclic),
  SectionText := concat([
    '## Value-flow reachability\n',
    '\n',
    'Transitive closure over `df_edge`, computed by the mutual `df_reach` /\n',
    '`df_hop` pair, keyed on the whole `(span, kind)` node identity. Every edge\n',
    'is intra-procedural, so a component never crosses a callable.\n',
    '`self-reaching` counts nodes with a path back to themselves: ', Cyclic, '\n',
    'of them over ', Pairs, ' reachable pairs. Value flow inside one callable is\n',
    'a DAG, so any row above zero is a defect, not a measurement.\n',
    '\n',
    '| file | df edges | reachable pairs | self-reaching nodes |\n',
    '|---|--:|--:|--:|\n',
    Body, '\n']).

report_markdown(3, 'procs', SectionText) <-
  proc_table(Body),
  SectionText := concat([
    '## Widest callables\n',
    '\n',
    'Ranked by df value nodes owned, competition ranking, cut at rank 25.\n',
    'A callable owns a value node when it is the innermost callable whose span\n',
    'contains it. `chain depth` is the capped ladder; see the next section.\n',
    '\n',
    '| file | callable | df nodes | df edges | chain depth |\n',
    '|---|---|--:|--:|--:|\n',
    Body, '\n']).

report_markdown(4, 'depth', SectionText) <-
  depth_table(Body),
  SectionText := concat([
    '## Chain-depth histogram\n',
    '\n',
    'Longest chain from a root (a value node no edge targets) to each node a\n',
    'callable owns. The ladder carries a `Level < 32` termination guard; the\n',
    'graph is acyclic, so it converges below the guard and a reported depth is\n',
    'the measured chain, not a saturation floor.\n',
    '\n',
    '| chain depth | callables |\n',
    '|--:|--:|\n',
    Body, '\n']).

report_markdown(5, 'span-identity', SectionText) <-
  alias_table(Body),
  total_aliased(Aliased),
  SectionText := concat([
    '## Span identity across the wire\n',
    '\n',
    'A df node is `(span, kind)`. `src/lang/rust.rs` df_push stores each value\n',
    "node's full extent and `FlatFact::Edge` names `from_kind`/`to_kind`\n",
    'beside the endpoint spans, so both halves cross the wire and every rel in\n',
    'this rail keys on both.\n',
    '\n',
    '`aliased spans` counts spans carrying more than one kind: ', Aliased, '\n',
    'over the corpus. An implicit `ret` covers the tail expression it returns,\n',
    'which is what those are; the kind separates them and the closure above\n',
    'stays acyclic. A span-only consumer would merge exactly these.\n',
    '\n',
    '`df node rows` is the `df_node` REL, which is a set, so two facts that agree\n',
    'on span and kind are already one row here.\n',
    '\n',
    '| file | df node rows | distinct spans | aliased spans |\n',
    '|---|--:|--:|--:|\n',
    Body, '\n']).

report_markdown(6, 'todo', SectionText) <-
  total_df_edges(Edges),
  SectionText := concat([
    '## Not built yet\n',
    '\n',
    '| construct | where | state |\n',
    '|---|---|---|\n',
    '| interprocedural value flow | `sprefa-extract/src/types.rs` `DfEdgeKind` | TODO. Only `Direct` exists; the `Flow` union (arg to param, ret to call_res, higher-order) is commented out and marked PENDING. All ', Edges, ' edges in this report are intra-procedural. |\n',
    '| full-extent df spans for go and kotlin | `src/lang/go.rs` / `src/lang/kotlin.rs` df_push | TODO. Both still push `len: 0`, so a .go or .kt corpus merges value nodes at one offset the way the Rust lift did before `issues/df-span-identity-aliasing`. |\n',
    '| endpoint kinds on the df arg/param arms | `types.rs` `FlatFact::DfArg` / `FlatFact::DfParam` | TODO. The edge arm names `from_kind`/`to_kind`; the aux arms name spans only, so a consumer joining an argument slot back to a node has the same merge. |\n',
    '| a file written from dl6 | fs effects | TODO. This document is written by `v6/dl/dataflow/report-extract.sh`, which queries `report_markdown` in section order. |\n']).

? report_markdown(section_ordinal, section_name, section_text).
